# File: tests/features/vault-everywhere.feature
# Generated from: specs/19-store-provider-credentials-in-the-encrypted-vault-on-every-os/requirements.md
Feature: Provider credentials in the encrypted vault on every OS

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: The vault stores credentials on <platform>
    Given a faked engine for "<platform>"
    When a credential for "opencode-go/default" is saved, read, listed and deleted through the credential store
    Then "vault.json" and "vault.key" are written under "<directory>"
    And "vault.json" holds ciphertext and not the secret
    And the read returns the saved secret and the list returns "opencode-go/default"
    And after the delete "vault.json" has no "opencode-go/default" entry
    And no "security", "powershell.exe" or "secret-tool" process runs

    Examples:
      | platform | directory                                            |
      | macos    | /Users/tester/Library/Application Support/nmg-router |
      | windows  | C:\Users\tester\AppData\Local\nmg-router             |
      | linux    | /home/tester/.local/share/nmg-router                 |
      | other    | /home/tester/.local/share/nmg-router                 |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Vault protections hold on POSIX
    Given a faked Linux engine
    When the first credential is saved through the credential store
    Then the directory is created with mode 700 before any write
    And each written vault file is set to mode 600
    And a failing directory step raises "vault_failed" with nothing written
    And a malformed "vault.key" beside existing entries raises "vault_failed" and is not regenerated

  @SCN003
  Scenario: No keyring code remains
    Given the change is complete
    When the source and tests are inspected
    Then no keyring backend module, keyring routing, keyring simulation, "keyring_locked", "keyring_failed" or "NoKeyringError" remains

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Callers see the same store
    Given code that uses createCredentialStore
    When it saves, reads, lists and deletes credentials, and tries to save an "anthropic" credential
    Then the operations behave as before, the "anthropic" save is refused with no process run or file written, and the sentinel secret reaches no recorded surface

  @SCN005
  Scenario: README describes the vault on every OS
    Given the README "Credential security" section
    When it is read
    Then it says credentials are kept in the encrypted vault on every OS with each OS's directory and the hardening steps
    And it does not mention Keychain, Credential Manager, Secret Service, secret-tool or libsecret
